## Technical Architecture & Subsystems

1. **Morton-Ordered Octree Spatial Builder ($\mathcal{O}(N \log N)$)**  
   Transforms high-dimensional coordinate datasets into a highly optimized, linear Z-order space-filling curve. This maximizes L1/L2 hardware cache locality across distributed GPU memories during short-range tree traversals.

2. **CUDA-Accelerated Tree-PM Force & $\nabla\epsilon$ Solver**  
   A single-pass, warp-optimized device kernel executing non-recursive tree walks inside shared memory. It calculates Newtonian gravity alongside the explicit $\nabla\epsilon$ work-energy tensor to preserve Hamiltonian invariants.

3. **Symplectic Power-of-Two Leapfrog Coordinator**  
   Implements a phase-locked Kick-Drift-Kick (KDK) integration pipeline with nested time-bin hierarchies ($\Delta t_n = \Delta t_0 / 2^n$). Particles drop down to micro-timesteps in dense galactic cores and promotion/demotion gates are restricted strictly to synchronous macro-steps to maintain total system energy drift below $\Delta E / E_0 < 10^{-5}$.

4. **Orthogonal Recursive Bisection (ORB) Balancer**  
   Dynamically partitions simulation box space across distributed MPI process domains. By using `std::nth_element` selection to split domains at absolute particle count medians rather than raw spatial geometry, it guarantees true compute-load equilibrium as clustering accelerates down to $z=0$.

5. **CUDA-Aware MPI InfiniBand Communications**  
   Bypasses host CPU staging layers completely. Utilizing GPUDirect RDMA, boundary halo particles are streamed directly from GPU VRAM to GPU VRAM using an event-driven synchronization design to protect against pipeline memory races.

6. **Parallel HDF5 MPI-IO Snapshot Exporter**  
   Eliminates the serialization bottleneck via collective hyperslab selection. All nodes pool data sizes through parallel scans and dump distributed coordinates into a single, shared binary file concurrently with zero data loss.

7. **Tree-Accelerated $\xi(r)$ Analyzer Post-Processor**  
   An advanced diagnostic utility leveraging the spatial octree structure to prune distant bounding boxes, accelerating two-point correlation pair counting down to $\mathcal{O}(N \log N)$ performance for strict observational benchmarking.

